-- houthis-advance-aden-yemen-forces-fall-back-20261119 (news; English 649 words; Nepali 408 words)
INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt")
VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'houthis-advance-aden-yemen-forces-fall-back-20261119', 'news', 'Yemen',
'Houthis Advance on Aden as Yemen Forces Fall Back',
'येमेनी सेना पछि हटेपछि हुथीहरू अदनतर्फ अघि बढे',
'The Houthis advance on Aden after Saudi-backed forces pulled back to defend the port city, leaving the group about 100 km from the seat of government.',
'साउदी समर्थित सेना बन्दरगाह शहरको रक्षाका लागि पछि हटेपछि हुथीहरू अदनतर्फ अघि बढे, सरकारको केन्द्रबाट करिब १०० किलोमिटर नजिक पुगे।',
$$<p>The Houthis advance on Aden gathered pace on Monday 16 November, after Saudi-backed government forces fell back from the southern coast to defend the port city, the seat of Yemen internationally recognised government.</p><p>Houthi fighters reached Khor Omairh, about 100 km west of Aden, and stood 25 km from government lines at Qawah, five Yemeni military sources told <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/houthis-seize-ground-yemens-southern-coast-edge-closer-aden-2026-11-16/">Reuters</a>. Residents said checkpoints had gone up across Aden and identity checks were under way.</p><h2>Houthis advance on Aden at a glance</h2><table><tr><th>Detail</th><th>Information</th></tr><tr><td>Advance</td><td>Houthi fighters reached Khor Omairh, 100 km west of Aden, on 16 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Nearest front line</td><td>25 km from government lines at Qawah, on the coast</td></tr><tr><td>Government move</td><td>Forces withdrew from areas near the Bab el-Mandeb Strait to defend Aden</td></tr><tr><td>City under threat</td><td>Aden, the government seat of power since the Houthis took Sanaa in 2014</td></tr><tr><td>Other front</td><td>Government forces besieged in Taiz, Yemen third biggest city</td></tr></table><h2>What happened</h2><p>Following a counter-attack by its forces in October, the Yemeni government said on Sunday it was withdrawing from areas near the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a global shipping artery, to focus on defending Aden. The Houthis then seized swathes of territory along the southern coast, according to military sources who spoke to <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/houthis-seize-ground-yemens-southern-coast-edge-closer-aden-2026-11-16/">Reuters</a>.</p><p>The withdrawal marks a big setback in the Saudi-backed campaign against the Iran-allied group, which has been firing ballistic missiles at Saudi airports and oil facilities since the Yemen war restarted. The government focus is now to secure Aden and the province of Lahj, three government sources said, while its forces redeploy and reorganise along front lines to prepare for the recapture of areas seized by the Houthis.</p><p>Yemen civil war had been dormant since 2022 until it reignited this summer as a spillover of the Iran war. The Houthis made rapid gains to capture the coast along the Red Sea and the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, while besieging government forces in Taiz, in mountains above the approach to Aden. Saudi-backed forces retook key positions around the strait, notably Dhubab, in an offensive last month, but they were unable to drive the Houthis entirely away or to retake the city of al-Mocha further up the coast.</p><p>In Aden, government employee Amin Mahmoud told <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/houthis-seize-ground-yemens-southern-coast-edge-closer-aden-2026-11-16/">Reuters</a> by phone that food and fuel were available, but people were worried about the retreat of government forces and the possibility of fighting drawing closer to the city. The gains in Yemen and attacks on Saudi Arabia and Red Sea shipping have enhanced Iran position in the wider Middle East conflict launched by the United States and Israel in February, <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/houthis-seize-ground-yemens-southern-coast-edge-closer-aden-2026-11-16/">Reuters</a> reported. That wider war also frames the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/iran-linked-assassination-plot-greece-north-macedonia-20261118">Iran-linked plot reported in Greece and North Macedonia</a>, while the fighting in Ukraine shows how front lines can shift fast, as in the <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ukraine-strikes-crimean-bridge-second-day-record-drones-20261118">second day of strikes on the Crimean bridge</a>.</p><h2>Why it matters</h2><p>Aden is the last major seat of the internationally recognised government. One analyst, Mohammed Al-Qadhi, told <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/houthis-seize-ground-yemens-southern-coast-edge-closer-aden-2026-11-16/">Reuters</a> there was a serious threat to the city, calling the retreat a major setback. The government had aimed to recapture Sanaa, he said, but now it is defending Aden. The fragmented state of government forces, weakened by years of disagreements and infighting, is working in the Houthis favour, he added.</p><p>The stakes go beyond Yemen. The Bab el-Mandeb Strait controls access to the Red Sea, one of the busiest shipping lanes in the world, so a Houthi grip on the coast raises the risk for global trade as well as for Saudi Arabia, which has been drawn back into confrontation with the group.</p><h2>What is not confirmed</h2><p>The exact positions of the front lines have not been independently verified, and the reports rest on five Yemeni military sources and three government sources who spoke to <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/houthis-seize-ground-yemens-southern-coast-edge-closer-aden-2026-11-16/">Reuters</a>. It is not confirmed whether the Houthis intend to capture Aden outright or to hold their ground, and the government claim that its forces are reorganising to retake lost areas has not been tested on the ground.</p><h2>Sources</h2><p>Coverage: <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/houthis-seize-ground-yemens-southern-coast-edge-closer-aden-2026-11-16/">Reuters</a>, 16 November 2026.</p>$$,
$$<p>साउदी समर्थित सरकारी सेना दक्षिणी तटबाट पछि हटेर बन्दरगाह शहरको रक्षा गर्न थालेपछि सोमबार १६ नोभेम्बरमा हुथीहरू अदनतर्फ अघि बढे। अदन येमेनको अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय मान्यता प्राप्त सरकारको केन्द्र हो।</p><p>पाँच येमेनी सैन्य स्रोतहरूले रोयटर्सलाई बताएअनुसार हुथी लडाकुहरू अदनबाट करिब १०० किलोमिटर पश्चिममा रहेको खोर ओमैरह पुगे र कावाहमा सरकारी रेखाबाट २५ किलोमिटर टाढा छन्। अदनका बासिन्दाहरूले शहरभरि चेकपोस्ट राखिएको र परिचयपत्र जाँच भइरहेको बताए।</p><h2>अदनतर्फ हुथी अग्रसरता एक नजरमा</h2><table><tr><th>विवरण</th><th>जानकारी</th></tr><tr><td>अग्रसरता</td><td>१६ नोभेम्बर २०२६ मा हुथी लडाकुहरू अदनबाट १०० किलोमिटर पश्चिम खोर ओमैरह पुगे</td></tr><tr><td>नजिकको मोर्चा</td><td>तटमा रहेको कावाहमा सरकारी रेखाबाट २५ किलोमिटर टाढा</td></tr><tr><td>सरकारी कदम</td><td>सेनाले बाब अल-मन्देब जलसन्धि नजिकका क्षेत्रबाट फिर्ता भएर अदनको रक्षा गर्ने निर्णय गर्‍यो</td></tr><tr><td>खतरामा रहेको शहर</td><td>अदन, हुथीहरूले २०१४ मा साना कब्जा गरेपछि सरकारको केन्द्र</td></tr><tr><td>अर्को मोर्चा</td><td>येमेनको तेस्रो ठूलो शहर ताइजमा सरकारी सेना घेराबन्दीमा</td></tr></table><h2>के भयो</h2><p>अक्टोबरमा आफ्नो सेनाको जवाफी आक्रमणपछि येमेनी सरकारले आइतबार विश्वव्यापी ढुवानी मार्ग बाब अल-मन्देब जलसन्धि नजिकका क्षेत्रबाट फिर्ता भएर अदनको रक्षामा ध्यान दिने बताएको थियो। त्यसपछि हुथीहरूले दक्षिणी तटमा ठूलो क्षेत्र कब्जा गरे।</p><p>यो फिर्ती इरान समर्थित समूहविरुद्धको साउदी समर्थित अभियानमा ठूलो धक्का हो। येमेन युद्ध पुनः सुरु भएपछि हुथीहरूले साउदी विमानस्थल र तेल सुविधाहरूमा ब्यालिस्टिक मिसाइल प्रहार गर्दै आएका छन्। सरकारको ध्यान अब अदन र लहज प्रान्त सुरक्षित गर्नु हो, र सेना हराएका क्षेत्र फिर्ता लिन मोर्चामा पुनः संगठित हुँदैछ।</p><p>येमेनको गृहयुद्ध २०२२ देखि शान्त थियो, तर यस गर्मीमा इरान युद्धको असरले पुनः सुरु भयो। हुथीहरूले रातो सागर र बाब अल-मन्देब जलसन्धिको तट कब्जा गर्दै ताइजमा सरकारी सेनालाई घेराबन्दीमा पारे। साउदी समर्थित सेनाले गत महिना धुबाबलगायत प्रमुख स्थान फिर्ता लियो, तर हुथीहरूलाई पूर्ण रूपमा हटाउन वा अल-मोखा शहर फिर्ता लिन सकेन।</p><p>अदनका सरकारी कर्मचारी अमिन महमुदले रोयटर्सलाई फोनमा खाद्यान्न र इन्धन उपलब्ध रहेको, तर सरकारी सेनाको पछि हटाइ र लडाइँ शहर नजिक आउने सम्भावनाले मानिसहरू चिन्तित रहेको बताए।</p><h2>किन महत्त्वपूर्ण छ</h2><p>अदन अन्तर्राष्ट्रिय मान्यता प्राप्त सरकारको अन्तिम प्रमुख केन्द्र हो। विश्लेषक मोहम्मद अल-कादीले रोयटर्सलाई शहरमा गम्भीर खतरा रहेको र यो फिर्ती ठूलो धक्का भएको बताए। सरकारको लक्ष्य साना फिर्ता लिनु थियो, तर अब अदनको रक्षा गर्नुपरेको छ। वर्षौंदेखिको मतभेद र आन्तरिक कलहले कमजोर सरकारी सेनाको अवस्थाले हुथीहरूलाई फाइदा पुगेको उनले बताए।</p><p>यसको असर येमेनभन्दा बाहिर पनि छ। बाब अल-मन्देब जलसन्धिले विश्वको व्यस्ततम ढुवानी मार्ग रातो सागरको पहुँच नियन्त्रण गर्छ, त्यसैले तटमा हुथी पकडले विश्व व्यापार र साउदी अरब दुवैका लागि जोखिम बढाउँछ।</p><h2>के पुष्टि भएको छैन</h2><p>मोर्चाको ठ्याक्कै स्थान स्वतन्त्र रूपमा प्रमाणित भएको छैन; रिपोर्ट रोयटर्ससँग कुरा गरेका पाँच सैन्य र तीन सरकारी स्रोतमा आधारित छ। हुथीहरूले अदन नै कब्जा गर्ने इरादा राखेका हुन् वा आफ्नो स्थानमा रहने हुन् भन्ने पुष्टि भएको छैन, र हराएका क्षेत्र फिर्ता लिने सरकारी दाबी मैदानमा परीक्षण भएको छैन।</p><h2>स्रोतहरू</h2><p>रिपोर्ट: <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/houthis-seize-ground-yemens-southern-coast-edge-closer-aden-2026-11-16/">Reuters</a>, १६ नोभेम्बर २०२६।</p>$$,
